description:
Owner report (2026-11-18): with per-task folders, hook folders accumulate after hook failures. A frame of task "NGC 7000" was saved as
/home/rumen/indigo_image_cache/Shutdown/Shutdown/NGC 7000/NGC7000_2026-11-18_Light_Filter #1_idx004_....fits
i.e. the Imager Agent's CCD_LOCAL_MODE.DIR was left at the folder of the Shutdown hook (twice), and the next START captured that as the original folder (capture_original()), so every later folder hangs off it. The owner observes it when hooks fail ("the hooks do not restore the directory at failure").

Reading the code, every finish path (finish_hook, finish_task, finish_stop, process_starting timeout, process_running "Scripting Agent disappeared", process_stopping timeout) calls restore_context(), which sends CCD_LOCAL_MODE DIR/OBJECT = original_dir/original_object. So the cause is not an obviously missing call. Candidates to check:
- the restore request is sent but lost, rejected or overwritten afterwards (e.g. Sequencer.js failure/abort handling, the Imager Agent or the CCD driver while busy or in Alert, a CCD_LOCAL_MODE Alert after the failure);
- capture_original() on START reads observed->imager_dir before the restore's update arrives, or the observed value is stale;
- original_valid / context_applied handling across stop_scheduler(), restore_context() and a following hook (SHUTDOWN after a failed task/hook, STARTUP after a failed SHUTDOWN, START during SHUTDOWN, STOP_TIMEOUT path that stops without restore of a later hook);
- a hook that fails before or right after its sequence starts.

Work: reproduce first with an integration test in indigo_test/integration/test_agent_scheduler.c (a failing hook, then START again and a task, checking the Imager Agent DIR), find the real root cause, fix it in the scheduler (or where the cause is), and keep the Imager Agent DIR from ever being captured as an original folder when it is a folder the scheduler itself set. Add regression tests for the failing STARTUP and SHUTDOWN hooks and a failing task followed by the SHUTDOWN hook, each followed by a new START. Update SCHEDULER.md / INDIGO_SCHEDULER_GUIDE.md if the documented behaviour changes. Bump the version of every fixed driver.
